			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement DNS diagnostic and health-check IPC commands\n\nIntroduce a complete suite of Tauri commands under `Source/Binary/Build/DnsCommands/` to expose the internal DNS server state to the Wind/Sky frontend for diagnostic and monitoring purposes. This implements the backend support for a DNS health dashboard and resolution tester.\n\nThe commit adds:\n- **DTOs:** `DnsHealthStatus`, `DnsServerInfo`, `DnsResolutionResult`, `ZoneInfo`, `ZoneRecord`, and `ForwardAllowList` to structure return payloads, adhering to PascalCase naming.\n- **Server Info & Startup:** `dns_get_server_info` returns port status and a persistent startup timestamp captured via `StartupTime`.\n- **Health Monitoring:** `dns_get_health_status` and `dns_health_check` provide aggregated health snapshots and boolean checks for the server, zone, and forwarder states.\n- **Zone Inspection:** `dns_get_zone_info` returns the static `editor.land` authoritative zone snapshot, including SOA, NS, A records, and DNSSEC keys/signatures.\n- **Resolution Logic:** `dns_resolve` handles manual queries, routing `editor.land` to `127.0.0.1` and allowlisted external domains to `TEST-NET-1` placeholders, while rejecting others.\n- **Helpers:** `dns_get_forward_allowlist` and `dns_test_resolution` provide simplified access for automated health loops.\n\nAll commands gate access on the `DnsPort` state, ensuring safe interaction with the underlying Hickory DNS server lifecycle.",
			"SHA": "004e560b79b0d6cb9ff67b09d4f9de615720c1a3"
		},
